{"qid":"Q334","names":["Republic of Singapore"],"title":"Republic of Singapore","endonym":{"native":"Republic of Singapore","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Singapore became an independent republic on 9 August 1965 after separation from Malaysia, a departure the founding prime minister Lee Kuan Yew described as a moment of personal anguish. Under the People's Action Party, which has governed without interruption since self-government in 1959, Singapore transformed from a colonial entrepôt with high unemployment into one of the world's wealthiest states per capita, driven by export manufacturing, container shipping, finance, and, later, pharmaceuticals and integrated resorts. Goh Chok Tong succeeded Lee in 1990 and Lee Hsien Loong in 2004; Lawrence Wong assumed the premiership in 2024. The city-state of 733 km² has periodically expanded through land reclamation and as of the dataset's end remains among the most densely populated sovereign states on earth.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Modern sovereign city-state; boundaries are precisely defined and reclamation extents are well-documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Singapore","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Singapore"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Singapore","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore"}],"britannica":"place/Singapore","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Singapore","rulers":[{"qid":"Q131248","name":"Lee Kuan Yew","start":1959,"end":1990,"image":"Lee Kuan Yew.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Lee%20Kuan%20Yew.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Robert D. Ward","at